With these in place:

– `<TableContainer {...getTableContainerProps()} title="Foo" description="Bar">…`  
  will render a `<div id="data-table-X">` containing  
  `<h4 id="data-table-X__title">Foo</h4>` and  
  `<p id="data-table-X__description">Bar</p>`.  

– You can then render your table as  
  `<Table {...getTableProps()} aria-labelledby="data-table-X__title" aria-describedby="data-table-X__description">…</Table>`  
  (or manage it however your render‐prop consumer prefers).  

This makes the visible title/description nodes referenceable via ARIA and fixes the JAWS labeling issue.
